# Who must approve a pull request, by path. With the branch rule "Require review from Code
# Owners" switched on, a pull request cannot merge until an owner of every file it touches
# has approved it. This file is how production is controlled.
#
# Later lines win over earlier ones.
#
# This repository has one maintainer, so one person holds all three roles below. In a team
# these would be three different groups (@org/platform, @org/developers, @org/release-approvers),
# and that separation is the point: the person who writes a change is not the one who
# approves it for production.

# The platform: charts, add-on versions, the promotion scripts and this file itself.
*                       @sabiut

# dev has no owner line: the release bot's pull requests merge by themselves once the
# checks pass.
/envs/dev/

# stg: any developer on the team may approve.
/envs/stg/              @sabiut

# prd: only release approvers. The bot can open the pull request; it cannot approve it.
/envs/prd/              @sabiut
